@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Running Automated Tests in Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Automated testing in Azure DevOps Pipelines ensures **code quality, stability, and reliability** before deployment. By integrating unit, integration, and UI tests, teams can catch defects early and streamline their CI/CD workflows.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Automated Testing in Pipelines?</h2>
        <p>Automated testing in Azure Pipelines enables teams to execute test cases **automatically** as part of the Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) process.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Ensures **code correctness** before deployment.</li>
            <li>Speeds up the development lifecycle by **reducing manual testing efforts**.</li>
            <li>Improves **software reliability** by catching issues early.</li>
            <li>Enables **parallel test execution** for faster feedback.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/test-automation.png" alt="Automated Testing Workflow" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Automated Testing Workflow in Azure Pipelines</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Types of Automated Tests</h4>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Unit Tests:</strong> Verify individual components or functions.</li>
                <li><strong>Integration Tests:</strong> Ensure different modules work together correctly.</li>
                <li><strong>UI Tests:</strong> Simulate user interactions in applications.</li>
                <li><strong>Load & Performance Tests:</strong> Test how the system behaves under heavy traffic.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Setting Up Automated Tests in Azure Pipelines</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to integrate automated testing into Azure DevOps Pipelines:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Add Test Framework Dependencies:</strong> Install necessary test libraries (e.g., NUnit, JUnit, Selenium).</li>
            <li><strong>Write Test Cases:</strong> Develop test scripts for unit, integration, or UI testing.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure Test Execution in YAML Pipeline:</strong> Define test tasks in the pipeline.</li>
            <li><strong>Analyze Test Results:</strong> View test execution reports in Azure DevOps.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML Pipeline for Automated Testing</h4>
            <pre>
trigger:
  - main

jobs:
  - job: Test
    steps:
      - task: UseDotNet@2
        inputs:
          packageType: 'sdk'
          version: '6.x'

      - script: dotnet test --logger trx
        displayName: 'Run Unit Tests'

      - task: PublishTestResults@2
        inputs:
          testResultsFormat: 'VSTest'
          testResultsFiles: '**/*.trx'
          mergeTestResults: true
          failTaskOnFailedTests: true
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/test-reports.png" alt="Test Results in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Viewing Test Results in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Running Automated Tests</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **test categories** to separate unit, integration, and UI tests.</li>
            <li>Enable **parallel test execution** for faster feedback.</li>
            <li>Fail the pipeline if critical tests fail.</li>
            <li>Store test artifacts and logs for debugging failed tests.</li>
            <li>Integrate with **Azure Test Plans** for manual and exploratory testing.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Running automated tests in Azure DevOps Pipelines enhances **software quality, reliability, and deployment confidence**. By integrating unit, integration, and UI testing, teams can detect and fix issues early in the development lifecycle.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Introduction to Release Pipelines in Azure DevOps**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntegratingAzureReposGitHub", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Integrating with Azure Repos & GitHub</a>
    </div>
</div>
